{
  "id": 531504076,
  "iid": 26507,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: Fix the Lua debugger build without libpcap",
  "description": "LuaDebuggerCaptureSuppression::onCaptureSessionEvent() is registered\nwith capture_callback_add() only when HAVE_LIBPCAP is defined, and it is\nthe sole caller of enter() and exit(). Without libpcap all three are\ndefined in an anonymous namespace but never referenced, so GCC reports\n-Wunused-function for each of them and the -Werror build fails:\n\n    lua_debugger_dialog.cpp:229:6: error: 'static void\n    {anonymous}::LuaDebuggerCaptureSuppression::onCaptureSessionEvent(int,\n    _capture_session*, void*)' defined but not used\n    [-Werror=unused-function]\n\nPut the declarations and definitions of the three functions under the\nsame HAVE_LIBPCAP conditional as their registration, which also makes\nthe #else branch inside onCaptureSessionEvent() unnecessary.\n\nisActive(), reconcileOnStartup() and setPrevEnabled() stay\nunconditional: the dialog calls them either way, and without libpcap\nsuppression simply never becomes active.",
  "state": "merged",
